### CW-002L
Arbitrary bistochastic step \(P\) admits a symmetric reversible two-microstep lift:

\[
A(P)=\begin{pmatrix}0&P\\P^\top&0\end{pmatrix},
\qquad
K=\begin{pmatrix}0&I\\I&0\end{pmatrix},
\]

with

\[
A(P)K=\operatorname{diag}(P,P^\top).
\]

After a positive shell, every microstep is positive symmetric doubly stochastic.

This gives undecidability under a forced alternating reversible schedule.

